        "content": "# Quick Build: Ultra-Performant JSON Validation Script\n\n## Summary\nAdd an ultra-performant JSON validation module to the project. The module provides a high-performance JSON validator that uses streaming-style single-pass character scanning to validate JSON structure without constructing an AST or intermediate objects. Includes a CLI entry point for validating JSON files/stdin and co-located tests.\n\n## Scope\nSmall\n\n## Files Affected\n- `src/json-validator.ts` (new) - Core validation module with performant single-pass validator\n- `src/validate-json.ts` (new) - CLI script entry point for validating JSON files or stdin\n- `src/json-validator.test.ts` (new) - Comprehensive tests for the validator\n\n## Tasks\n\n### Task 1: Create the core JSON validation module\n- **ID**: QB-1\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Files**: `src/json-validator.ts`\n- **Description**: Create an ultra-performant JSON validation module that uses character-by-character scanning with a manual state machine. The validator should avoid JSON.parse overhead by not constructing objects — it only validates structure. Key performance characteristics: zero allocations during validation (pre-allocated state stack), single-pass O(n) scanning, no regex usage, no intermediate string construction. The module should export: `validateJson(input: string): ValidationResult` where ValidationResult contains `valid: boolean`, `error?: string`, and `position?: number`. Also export a `validateJsonFast(input: string): boolean` that returns only a boolean for maximum speed (skips error message construction). Support full JSON spec: objects, arrays, strings (with escape sequences), numbers (including scientific notation), booleans, null, and nested structures.\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Exports `validateJson` function returning `{ valid, error?, position? }`\n  - Exports `validateJsonFast` function returning boolean only\n  - Single-pass character scanning with no intermediate allocations\n  - Validates all JSON types: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null\n  - Handles nested structures with pre-allocated stack\n  - Properly validates string escape sequences including `\\uXXXX`\n  - Rejects invalid JSON with descriptive error messages and position info\n  - TypeScript strict mode, camelCase functions, PascalCase types\n  - No external dependencies\n\n### Task 2: Create the CLI entry point script\n- **ID**: QB-2\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Files**: `src/validate-json.ts`\n- **Description**: Create a CLI script that uses the json-validator module to validate JSON from file arguments or stdin. Usage: `bun run src/validate-json.ts [file.json]` or pipe via stdin. Should exit with code 0 for valid JSON, code 1 for invalid JSON, printing a clear message with error details on failure. Follow the same pattern as the existing `src/index.ts` entry point (using process.argv).\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Reads JSON from file argument or stdin\n  - Exits with code 0 for valid JSON, code 1 for invalid\n  - Prints validation result with error details and position on failure\n  - Follows existing entry point pattern from `src/index.ts`\n  - No external dependencies\n\n### Task 3: Create comprehensive tests\n- **ID**: QB-3\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Files**: `src/json-validator.test.ts`\n- **Description**: Create thorough tests for the JSON validator using Bun's test runner. Follow the existing test pattern from `src/utils.test.ts` using `describe`/`test`/`expect`. Cover: valid JSON for all types, invalid JSON cases, edge cases (empty strings, deeply nested, large numbers, unicode escapes), and performance characteristics. Test both `validateJson` and `validateJsonFast`.\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Uses `describe`/`test`/`expect` pattern from bun:test\n  - Tests valid JSON: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null\n  - Tests invalid JSON: trailing commas, unclosed brackets, bad escapes, etc.\n  - Tests edge cases: empty input, deeply nested structures, whitespace handling\n  - Tests both `validateJson` and `validateJsonFast` exports\n  - All tests pass with `bun test`\n"
